"""
One axle's hydraulic disc brakes: the caliper's fluid compliance and the friction torque its
pressure clamps onto the disc.

The friction, its sine ramp below `w0` and the shaft ports are
`Chassis.Brakes.PartialFrictionBrake`'s; `support` must be connected. `port` is the brake-fluid
connection.

Pressures are gauge: the caliper's pressure p is `port.p` less the ambient pressure `p_amb`, since
HydraulicComponents ports carry absolute pressure. A released circuit at ambient pressure leaves
the caliper empty and applies no torque. The admitted fluid volume V sets p. Up to the clearance
take-up volume `V0` the pads travel against a soft linear law, p = p0 V/V0, and apply no torque;
beyond it they press the disc, the stiffness rises cubically, p = p0 + K1 u + K3 u³ with
u = V - V0, and the friction torque magnitude is K (p - p0).

Assumptions: those of `PartialFrictionBrake`; the caliper starts empty, V = 0. `p_amb` defaults
to 100325 Pa, the reference pressure of `HydraulicComponents.IsothermalCompressible` and of
`VehicleComponents.DOT4`; set it to the reference of any other medium. The other defaults are a
front axle's, gauge (textbook).
"""
component Caliper
  extends VehicleComponents.Chassis.Brakes.PartialFrictionBrake(w0 = 0.2)
  "Brake-fluid connection"
  port = HydraulicComponents.Interfaces.Port() {^port}
  "Torque gain [N m/Pa]"
  parameter K::Real = 49.0e-5
  "Pad-contact pressure, gauge"
  parameter p0::Pressure = 0.5e5
  "Clearance take-up volume"
  parameter V0::Volume = 0.5e-6
  "Linear pressure-volume coefficient [Pa/m³]"
  parameter K1::Real = 1e12
  "Cubic pressure-volume coefficient [Pa/m⁹]"
  parameter K3::Real = 4.8e23
  "Ambient pressure, which a released caliper sits at"
  parameter p_amb::Pressure = 100325.0
  "Fluid volume admitted to the caliper"
  variable V::Volume = initial 0.0
  "Caliper pressure, gauge: above p_amb"
  variable p::Pressure
  "Fluid density at the caliper pressure"
  variable rho::Density
  "Volume beyond the clearance take-up"
  variable u::Volume
relations
  port.p = p_amb + p
  rho = HydraulicComponents.density(port.medium, port.p)
  der(V) = port.m_flow / rho
  u = V - V0
  p = ifelse(V < V0, p0 * V / V0, p0 + K1 * u + K3 * u ^ 3)
  tau = ifelse(V < V0, 0.0, K * (p - p0))
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Chassis/Brakes/Caliper.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "port": {
      "Dyad": {
        "placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "hydraulic_port_a", "x1": 450, "x2": 550, "y1": -50, "y2": 50, "rot": 270}}
      }
    }
  }
}
end
